<title>USA: Compaq to add 2,000 sales jobs - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Compaq to add 2,000 sales jobs - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compaq Computer Corp plans to hire 2,000 sales people in 1997 to improve its contact with customers, the Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Wednesday's electronic edition, the Journal said the increased sales force is related to Compaq's inability to acquire rival Gateway 2000 Inc. Compaq also plans to push its current distributors to improve service, the Journal said.</p>
<p>The Journal said that Compaq Chief Executive Eckhard Pfeiffer has told senior executives in the past few months that he believes the company is too distant from its customers.</p>
<p>In contrast, Gateway and other direct marketers have been increasing market share at a faster rate than Compaq.</p>
<p>Compaq plans to hire 1,000 sales people in the U.S. and 1,000 outside the U.S.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
